==Korean==

===Symbol===
'''ㅇㅜㄴ'''

# The original, Korean symbol consists of the Hangul letters ㅇ (ng), ㅜ (u), ㄴ (n).
# It is a [[fatigued]] or [[despaired]] emoticon, which represents a [[stick figure]] kneeling with the "ㅇ" being the head, the "ㅜ" being the arms and part of the body, and the "ㄴ" being part of the body and the legs.
# It can also be written with Latin letters using O, T and L.

====Synonyms====
* OTL
* orz

